<https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/eu-ai-act> a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "EU AI Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689) — obligation mapping"@en ;
    dct:description "OWL + SHACL projection of the substrate L3 EU AI Act mapping (docs/ns/eu-ai-act.ttl): the obligations most relevant to AI agents and tutors — for high-risk systems, risk management (Art. 9), data governance (Art. 10), record-keeping (Art. 12), transparency to deployers (Art. 13), human oversight (Art. 14) and accuracy and robustness (Art. 15); and, for any system that interacts with people, transparency to them (Art. 50). Composed into PGSL and projected here so a cited Article IRI dereferences, and an action record can name the obligation it is evidence for."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Independent formalization by Mark Spivey (Foxxi Mediums Inc.). Not affiliated with or endorsed by the European Union. Where this document and the published standard differ, the standard governs."@en ,
        "Mapped to the Interego substrate's EU AI Act vocabulary (prefix eu-ai-act:, docs/ns/eu-ai-act.ttl) by SKOS mappings: its Article individuals by exact match, and the evidence classes that realize an obligation by related match."@en ,
        "Each obligation is defined in the Regulation's terms. Whether a record is sufficient evidence of meeting one is for the provider, the deployer and the authorities to judge; this document only lets the record say which obligation it concerns."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/eu-ai-act/2026.10.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "2026.10.0" ;
    skos:historyNote "Versioned by calendar (YYYY.MM.PATCH) from 2026.10.0: the version numbers this document, not the standard it formalizes. Every released version stays resolvable at its version IRI, and the content there never changes. Earlier publications carried no version IRI, and their owl:versionInfo restated the version of the standard."@en ;
    dct:creator "Mark Spivey" ;
